\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Study pipeline (schematic readouts, not measured performance). (A) Data \& split: the donor-disjoint CELLxGENE training atlas and the train/held-out split. (B) Arms and models: reference arms (frozen, HVG/PCA) and the fine-tuning recipes that carry the main comparison (CE-naive, ordinal head, ordinal + continuity), across the three model families; LoRA and ordinal + LoRA are evaluated only in Figure~\ref {fig:spectrum}. (C) Domains: the in-corpus external holdout (GSE153515), post-cutoff out-of-corpus external test (GSE299152) and cross-tissue epidermis; coverage varies by model and domain. (D) Readouts: gradient fidelity ($\rho $); layer adjacency accuracy (LAA), the fraction of cells whose nearest other cell in Euclidean space has an identical or adjacent stage; and classification (macro-F1).}}{8}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:pipeline}{{1}{8}{Study pipeline (schematic readouts, not measured performance). (A) Data \& split: the donor-disjoint CELLxGENE training atlas and the train/held-out split. (B) Arms and models: reference arms (frozen, HVG/PCA) and the fine-tuning recipes that carry the main comparison (CE-naive, ordinal head, ordinal + continuity), across the three model families; LoRA and ordinal + LoRA are evaluated only in Figure~\ref {fig:spectrum}. (C) Domains: the in-corpus external holdout (GSE153515), post-cutoff out-of-corpus external test (GSE299152) and cross-tissue epidermis; coverage varies by model and domain. (D) Readouts: gradient fidelity ($\rho $); layer adjacency accuracy (LAA), the fraction of cells whose nearest other cell in Euclidean space has an identical or adjacent stage; and classification (macro-F1)}{figure.1}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Layer-resolved analysis localizes the collapse to upper transformer layers. Differentiation-gradient Spearman $\rho $ (y-axis) across hidden states L1--L12 (x-axis) for the Geneformer-based configurations (n = 14{,}775 in-corpus external holdout epithelial cells; three seeds per adapted arm). Color key: thick dark gray line, frozen Geneformer; blue line, CE-naive (seed mean over seeds 42, 123 and 456; n = 3, ddof = 0; shaded band = mean $\pm $ 1 population SD across seeds), with the individual seeds as thin lines. The gradient collapse under classification fine-tuning is head-proximal: early layers retain the gradient, while L5--L12 decay apart from a seed-driven rebound at L9. See also Figure S7 and Table S3.}}{9}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:layerwise}{{2}{9}{Layer-resolved analysis localizes the collapse to upper transformer layers. Differentiation-gradient Spearman $\rho $ (y-axis) across hidden states L1--L12 (x-axis) for the Geneformer-based configurations (n = 14{,}775 in-corpus external holdout epithelial cells; three seeds per adapted arm). Color key: thick dark gray line, frozen Geneformer; blue line, CE-naive (seed mean over seeds 42, 123 and 456; n = 3, ddof = 0; shaded band = mean $\pm $ 1 population SD across seeds), with the individual seeds as thin lines. The gradient collapse under classification fine-tuning is head-proximal: early layers retain the gradient, while L5--L12 decay apart from a seed-driven rebound at L9. See also Figure S7 and Table S3}{figure.2}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces External test performance by model arm (GSE153515, four classes; n = 14{,}775 epithelial cells from two donors). Adapted-arm values and CI limits are averaged across three seeds; intervals use donor-level bootstrap 95\% CIs. Reference arms are single runs (seed 42). LAA, layer adjacency accuracy; ECE, expected calibration error.}}{9}{table.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:external}{{1}{9}{External test performance by model arm (GSE153515, four classes; n = 14{,}775 epithelial cells from two donors). Adapted-arm values and CI limits are averaged across three seeds; intervals use donor-level bootstrap 95\% CIs. Reference arms are single runs (seed 42). LAA, layer adjacency accuracy; ECE, expected calibration error}{table.1}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Gene-program readouts across representations and expression classes. (A) Spearman $\rho $ between fixed gene-program scores and each representation's pseudotime axis in cornea (GSE153515; 14,775 cells). Stemness: TP63, KRT15, KRT19, NFIB, CDH3; differentiation: KRT12, KRT3. Adapted bars: means over seeds 42, 123, 456, $\pm $1 population SD (ddof = 0); frozen: single reference, 95\% cell-bootstrap interval. (B) Cornea stemness score along pseudotime deciles, one checkpoint per arm, no intervals. (C) Basal-program $\rho $ (KRT5, KRT14, COL17A1) in epidermis, GSE147424 (18,355 cells) and GSE202352 (14,461 cells); points are single seed-42 checkpoints, 95\% cell-bootstrap intervals. Arms: panel A shows frozen, CE-naive, ordinal head and ordinal + continuity (open marker); panels B--D show frozen, CE-naive and ordinal head. (D) Cycling program score by expression class, fixed class means without intervals; cornea PCNA, MCM2, MKI67, TOP2A, epidermis MKI67, PCNA.}}{10}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:bio}{{3}{10}{Gene-program readouts across representations and expression classes. (A) Spearman $\rho $ between fixed gene-program scores and each representation's pseudotime axis in cornea (GSE153515; 14,775 cells). Stemness: TP63, KRT15, KRT19, NFIB, CDH3; differentiation: KRT12, KRT3. Adapted bars: means over seeds 42, 123, 456, $\pm $1 population SD (ddof = 0); frozen: single reference, 95\% cell-bootstrap interval. (B) Cornea stemness score along pseudotime deciles, one checkpoint per arm, no intervals. (C) Basal-program $\rho $ (KRT5, KRT14, COL17A1) in epidermis, GSE147424 (18,355 cells) and GSE202352 (14,461 cells); points are single seed-42 checkpoints, 95\% cell-bootstrap intervals. Arms: panel A shows frozen, CE-naive, ordinal head and ordinal + continuity (open marker); panels B--D show frozen, CE-naive and ordinal head. (D) Cycling program score by expression class, fixed class means without intervals; cornea PCNA, MCM2, MKI67, TOP2A, epidermis MKI67, PCNA}{figure.3}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Same-corpus holdout: fine-tuning raises per-class F1 and annotation accuracy. Adapted models evaluated on GSE153515 (n = 14{,}775 epithelial cells, two donors); the differentiation-gradient collapse measured over the same runs is shown in Figure~\ref {fig:layerwise}. (A) Cell-type labels (external test). (B) Donor UMAP; fill alone encodes donor (donor\_1 filled, donor\_2 open, single hue). (C) CE-naive confusion matrix, row-normalized. (D) Per-class F1 across five model arms (frozen, CE-naive, ordinal head, ordinal + continuity, HVG/PCA; adapted arms are three-seed means $\pm $ 1 sample SD, reference arms are single runs with no interval); the TAC column shows F1 = 0 (n = 171; three-class sensitivity in Figure S9). Class supports: 3,423 LSC, 171 TAC (1.2\%), 6,698 basal and 4,483 differentiated cells. See also Figure S6.}}{11}{figure.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:external}{{4}{11}{Same-corpus holdout: fine-tuning raises per-class F1 and annotation accuracy. Adapted models evaluated on GSE153515 (n = 14{,}775 epithelial cells, two donors); the differentiation-gradient collapse measured over the same runs is shown in Figure~\ref {fig:layerwise}. (A) Cell-type labels (external test). (B) Donor UMAP; fill alone encodes donor (donor\_1 filled, donor\_2 open, single hue). (C) CE-naive confusion matrix, row-normalized. (D) Per-class F1 across five model arms (frozen, CE-naive, ordinal head, ordinal + continuity, HVG/PCA; adapted arms are three-seed means $\pm $ 1 sample SD, reference arms are single runs with no interval); the TAC column shows F1 = 0 (n = 171; three-class sensitivity in Figure S9). Class supports: 3,423 LSC, 171 TAC (1.2\%), 6,698 basal and 4,483 differentiated cells. See also Figure S6}{figure.4}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Differentiation-gradient Spearman $\rho $ across evaluation domains (Geneformer-V2-104M arms). Same-corpus adapted values are three-seed means (per-seed ranges in parentheses); out-of-corpus values are three-seed means $\pm $ SD; cross-tissue and frozen values are single runs. Ordinal head, ordinal loss alone; ordinal + continuity, ordinal head with the continuity term ($\lambda = 0.5$). Em dashes mark domains not evaluated; BH--FDR control applies to the same-corpus family.}}{12}{table.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:domains}{{2}{12}{Differentiation-gradient Spearman $\rho $ across evaluation domains (Geneformer-V2-104M arms). Same-corpus adapted values are three-seed means (per-seed ranges in parentheses); out-of-corpus values are three-seed means $\pm $ SD; cross-tissue and frozen values are single runs. Ordinal head, ordinal loss alone; ordinal + continuity, ordinal head with the continuity term ($\lambda = 0.5$). Em dashes mark domains not evaluated; BH--FDR control applies to the same-corpus family}{table.2}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces The collapse depends on the evaluation domain: a three-domain boundary map. Differentiation-gradient Spearman $\rho $ by evaluation domain and arm (frozen, CE-naive, ordinal head, ordinal + continuity). Same-corpus GSE153515 (n = 14{,}775 epithelial cells), out-of-corpus GSE299152 (n = 21{,}374) and cross-tissue epidermis GSE147424 (n = 18{,}355). Same-corpus adapted values are three-seed means whose interval is the full per-seed min--max range (seeds 42, 123, 456), with the individual seeds plotted as open circles; out-of-corpus adapted values are three-seed means $\pm $ 1 sample SD; frozen and cross-tissue adapted arms are single runs with no interval. The same-corpus CE-naive mean ($-0.008$) is labelled at the axis; ordinal + continuity is not evaluated on cross-tissue (n.e.).}}{12}{figure.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:domains}{{5}{12}{The collapse depends on the evaluation domain: a three-domain boundary map. Differentiation-gradient Spearman $\rho $ by evaluation domain and arm (frozen, CE-naive, ordinal head, ordinal + continuity). Same-corpus GSE153515 (n = 14{,}775 epithelial cells), out-of-corpus GSE299152 (n = 21{,}374) and cross-tissue epidermis GSE147424 (n = 18{,}355). Same-corpus adapted values are three-seed means whose interval is the full per-seed min--max range (seeds 42, 123, 456), with the individual seeds plotted as open circles; out-of-corpus adapted values are three-seed means $\pm $ 1 sample SD; frozen and cross-tissue adapted arms are single runs with no interval. The same-corpus CE-naive mean ($-0.008$) is labelled at the axis; ordinal + continuity is not evaluated on cross-tissue (n.e.)}{figure.5}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Cross-architecture spectrum of differentiation-gradient collapse. (A) Differentiation-gradient Spearman $\rho $ for Geneformer-V2-104M (GSE153515; n = 14{,}775), scGPT-human (van Zyl; n = 20{,}158) and CellPLM. Individual runs are points, a black tick marks the run mean, and the dotted line marks $\rho = 0$; Geneformer's official-budget row plots seeds 42, 123, 456. Colours: frozen dark grey; CE-naive blue (all CE rows); ordinal head green; LoRA pink-purple; ordinal + LoRA orange-red. Per-seed values: Tables S6--S11. (B) Validation-$\rho $ peaks for scGPT-human (seeds 42, 123, 456, 789, 2024); dotted connector marks the macro-F1 selection epoch. (C) CellPLM dose response, drawn as two stacked panels that share the log-epoch axis: macro-F1 (top; three-seed mean $\pm $ SD) and differentiation-gradient $\rho $ (bottom), for naive cross-entropy and ordinal + LoRA at 15 epochs and convergence; the vertical dashed guide marks the first budget whose mean macro-F1 reaches its plateau (epoch 30), and the horizontal dashed rule is the frozen reference.}}{13}{figure.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:spectrum}{{6}{13}{Cross-architecture spectrum of differentiation-gradient collapse. (A) Differentiation-gradient Spearman $\rho $ for Geneformer-V2-104M (GSE153515; n = 14{,}775), scGPT-human (van Zyl; n = 20{,}158) and CellPLM. Individual runs are points, a black tick marks the run mean, and the dotted line marks $\rho = 0$; Geneformer's official-budget row plots seeds 42, 123, 456. Colours: frozen dark grey; CE-naive blue (all CE rows); ordinal head green; LoRA pink-purple; ordinal + LoRA orange-red. Per-seed values: Tables S6--S11. (B) Validation-$\rho $ peaks for scGPT-human (seeds 42, 123, 456, 789, 2024); dotted connector marks the macro-F1 selection epoch. (C) CellPLM dose response, drawn as two stacked panels that share the log-epoch axis: macro-F1 (top; three-seed mean $\pm $ SD) and differentiation-gradient $\rho $ (bottom), for naive cross-entropy and ordinal + LoRA at 15 epochs and convergence; the vertical dashed guide marks the first budget whose mean macro-F1 reaches its plateau (epoch 30), and the horizontal dashed rule is the frozen reference}{figure.6}{}}
